98,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,9885,279,2629,315,279,1931,19703,315,400,87,61,19,481,220,23,15,87,481,220,18,21,284,220,15,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nFind the sum of the real roots of $x^4 - 80x - 36 = 0.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"5d147915091346df36c0dffc72baa24b9e6ebc9d7e5f82e6e8af90e595cc1e89"},"seconds":68.33745646476746,"seed":951265685993516842,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the sum of the real roots of the equation \\(x^4 - 80x - 36 = 0\\), we can start by looking for any obvious roots and then use properties of polynomials to help us solve the problem.\n\nFirst, let's test some simple values for \\(x\\):\n\n1. For \\(x = 0\\):\n   \\[\n   0^4 - 80 \\cdot 0 - 36 = -36 \\neq 0\n   \\]\n   So, \\(x = 0\\) is not a root.\n\n2. For \\(x = 1\\):\n   \\[\n   1^4 - 80 \\cdot 1 - 36 = 1 - 80 - 36 = -115 \\neq 0\n   \\]\n   So, \\(x = 1\\) is not a root.\n\n3. For \\(x = -1\\):\n   \\[\n   (-1)^4 - 80 \\cdot (-1) - 36 = 1 + 80 - 36 = 45 \\neq 0\n   \\]\n   So, \\(x = -1\\) is not a root.\n\n4. For \\(x = 2\\):\n   \\[\n   2^4 - 80 \\cdot 2 - 36 = 16 - 160 - 36 = -180 \\neq 0\n   \\]\n   So, \\(x = 2\\) is not a root.\n\n5. For \\(x = -2\\):\n   \\[\n   (-2)^4 - 80 \\cdot (-2) - 36 = 16 + 160 - 36 = 140 \\neq 0\n   \\]\n   So, \\(x = -2\\) is not a root.\n\n6. For \\(x = 3\\):\n   \\[\n   3^4 - 80 \\cdot 3 - 36 = 81 - 240 - 36 = -195 \\neq 0\n   \\]\n   So, \\(x = 3\\) is not a root.\n\n7. For \\(x = -3\\):\n   \\[\n   (-3)^4 - 80 \\cdot (-3) - 36 = 81 + 240 - 36 = 285 \\neq 0\n   \\]\n   So, \\(x = -3\\) is not a root.\n\n8. For \\(x = 4\\):\n   \\[\n   4^4 - 80 \\cdot 4 - 36 = 256 - 320 - 36 = -100 \\neq 0\n   \\]\n   So, \\(x = 4\\) is not a root.\n\n9. For \\(x = -4\\):\n   \\[\n   (-4)^4 - 80 \\cdot (-4) - 36 = 256 + 320 - 36 = 540 \\neq 0\n   \\]\n   So, \\(x = -4\\) is not a root.\n\n10. For \\(x = 6\\):\n    \\[\n    6^4 - 80 \\cdot 6 - 36 = 1296 - 480 - 36 = 780 \\neq 0\n    \\]\n    So, \\(x = 6\\) is not a root.\n\n11. For \\(x = -6\\):\n    \\[\n    (-6)^4 - 80 \\cdot (-6) - 36 = 1296 + 480 - 36 = 1740 \\neq 0\n    \\]\n    So, \\(x = -6\\) is not a root.\n\nGiven that none of the simple integer values are roots, we need to consider other methods. We can use numerical methods or graphing to find the roots. However, the problem asks for the sum of the real roots, and we can use the fact that the sum of the roots of a polynomial \\(x^4 + a_3 x^3 + a_2 x^2 + a_1 x + a_0 = 0\\) is given by \\(-a_3\\), but since there is no \\(x^3\\) term in our polynomial, \\(a_3 = 0\\). Therefore, the sum of the roots (both real and complex) is 0. Since the problem asks for the sum of the real roots, and knowing that the sum of all roots is 0, if there are any complex roots, they must come in conjugate pairs, and their sum is zero. Therefore, the sum of the real roots must be the remaining part of the total sum, which is also 0.\n\nThus, the sum of the real roots of the equation \\(x^4 - 80x - 36 = 0\\) is \\(\\boxed{0}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{0}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
